  "instance_name": "boxing_day_holiday",
  "label": "Boxing Day Holiday",
  "description": "A public holiday observed in many countries, particularly in the United Kingdom and Commonwealth nations, occurring on December 26th. It traditionally involves gift-giving, charitable donations, and sales, often associated with post-Christmas shopping and festivities. The term 'boxing' historically referred to the practice of placing gifts or money in boxes for servants or the poor, or for giving to tradespeople. This real-world holiday is the basis for the pun in the meme, which conflates the holiday with the sport of boxing.",
